(7403562, 1164860, 29011, '<td valign="top">A high percentage of the daytime dragons are mostly blue around here too. I find the odd red one in the Autumn. Damsels are also mostly blue. The really big dragons (with the green/blue stripes) go on patrol in the evenings. You can sometimes find them in the shade before. I find the little ones are less afraid of stalking photographers. I haven''t seen as many small ones this year. My cat caught a few, tsk tsk. Her evening routine. Only one fatality. She calls me when she finds one and has a hard time letting one go.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2015-09-08 12:41:07.</i></td>', 'A high percentage of the daytime dragons are mostly blue around here too. I find the odd red one in the Autumn. Damsels are also mostly blue. The really big dragons (with the green/blue stripes) go on patrol in the evenings. You can sometimes find them in the shade before. I find the little ones are less afraid of stalking photographers. I haven''t seen as many small ones this year. My cat caught a few, tsk tsk. Her evening routine. Only one fatality. She calls me when she finds one and has a hard time letting one go.', '2015-09-08 13:39:18.000000', '2015-09-08 13:41:07.000000', 0),
(7404086, 1165147, 113591, '<td valign="top">Well, I had to Google it. <br/>10 for the association.<br/>Socialites in slip-ons.<br/> <br/>If you just cropped the left another 1 cm, there would be equal canine and human legs. This is very important, so do not slip up like this again. Hehe.</td>', 'Well, I had to Google it. 10 for the association.Socialites in slip-ons. If you just cropped the left another 1 cm, there would be equal canine and human legs. This is very important, so do not slip up like this again. Hehe.', '2015-09-11 09:08:23.000000', NULL, 0),
