(7404123, 1164554, 113591, '<td valign="top">Tradimg notes with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=68504" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">tnun</a>, were you?<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1165683" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/2000-2999/2142/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1165683.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/2000-2999/2142/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1165683.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/2000-2999/2142/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1165683.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Tradimg notes with  tnun, were you? ', '2015-09-11 10:13:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7404158, 1165213, 25024, '<td valign="top">*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club*<br/> <br/>An excellent image assumed to meet the challenge.<br/> <br/>I''m glad this didn''t remain hidden! A great action shot, nice viewpoint and nice hint of motion and lovely muted tones throughout, definitely one of your best to date. It''s a shame you have had to crop a little off the wing but its not major but the rest of the composition is working really well. There is nice sharpness on the back of the pigeon, it would have been nice to have the same sharpness on the head but again its only marginally soft and perfectly acceptable.<br/> <br/>A great image that ought to have fared better than it did, can''t say I understand the title though, if its crucial to the image'' appreciation then this might explain why it didn''t do better, Sid.</td>', '*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club* An excellent image assumed to meet the challenge. I''m glad this didn''t remain hidden! A great action shot, nice viewpoint and nice hint of motion and lovely muted tones throughout, definitely one of your best to date. It''s a shame you have had to crop a little off the wing but its not major but the rest of the composition is working really well. There is nice sharpness on the back of the pigeon, it would have been nice to have the same sharpness on the head but again its only marginally soft and perfectly acceptable. A great image that ought to have fared better than it did, can''t say I understand the title though, if its crucial to the image'' appreciation then this might explain why it didn''t do better, Sid.', '2015-09-11 12:47:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7404160, 1165058, 25024, '<td valign="top">*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club*<br/> <br/>An excellent image that is assumed to meet the challenge.<br/> <br/>Infra red is usually interesting but doesn''t always work well with everything but it is here. Those lovely rich blues of the sky are amazing and working well against that bleached beach and the colours of the palms, its all wonderful. As for the composition, I disagree with your commenter, I think you have hit it spot on here, I much prefer it in this format. For me the only thing that really lets this down is that ugly light on the tree, I think it would be most beneficial to attack that with the cloning tool.<br/> <br/>Apologies for the late critique but thanks for a great entry, Sid</td>', '*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club* An excellent image that is assumed to meet the challenge. Infra red is usually interesting but doesn''t always work well with everything but it is here. Those lovely rich blues of the sky are amazing and working well against that bleached beach and the colours of the palms, its all wonderful. As for the composition, I disagree with your commenter, I think you have hit it spot on here, I much prefer it in this format. For me the only thing that really lets this down is that ugly light on the tree, I think it would be most beneficial to attack that with the cloning tool. Apologies for the late critique but thanks for a great entry, Sid', '2015-09-11 12:55:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(7404167, 1164776, 25024, '<td valign="top">*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club*<br/> <br/>An appealing image that is assumed to meet the challenge.<br/> <br/>An interesting landscape of this unusual rock formation, the colours are rich throughout and composition is generally quite good. At the left you have some quite intriguing background features that I think should either have been excluded or better still made a more significant part of the overall composition. I do like the skies there are some lovely cloud formations and colours. There is good detail throughout, as you say, helped by the overcast lighting.<br/> <br/>Thanks for an interesting entry, Sid</td>', '*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club* An appealing image that is assumed to meet the challenge. An interesting landscape of this unusual rock formation, the colours are rich throughout and composition is generally quite good. At the left you have some quite intriguing background features that I think should either have been excluded or better still made a more significant part of the overall composition. I do like the skies there are some lovely cloud formations and colours. There is good detail throughout, as you say, helped by the overcast lighting. Thanks for an interesting entry, Sid', '2015-09-11 13:26:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(7404187, 1165139, 25024, '<td valign="top">*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club*<br/> <br/>An interesting image that is assumed to meet the challenge<br/> <br/>An interesting structure that has added interest through the lighting from the golden hour of dawn. The mist rising from the water also adds atmosphere to the shot. I assue this is a rail bridge, it would have been nice to be able to include a train traversing it but there''s not a lot you can do to alter that is there. Its a shame the foreground lacks any real impact to the image and as such may have been excluded without detriment to the end result, its probably the only real change I would have made to the composition.<br/> <br/>Thanks for an interesting submission, Sid</td>', '*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club* An interesting image that is assumed to meet the challenge An interesting structure that has added interest through the lighting from the golden hour of dawn. The mist rising from the water also adds atmosphere to the shot. I assue this is a rail bridge, it would have been nice to be able to include a train traversing it but there''s not a lot you can do to alter that is there. Its a shame the foreground lacks any real impact to the image and as such may have been excluded without detriment to the end result, its probably the only real change I would have made to the composition. Thanks for an interesting submission, Sid', '2015-09-11 15:18:57.000000', NULL, 0);
